(version 1)
# Eurocircuits: only the limits that do NOT depend on the pattern class.
# Sources (read 2026-10-29):
#   https://www.eurocircuits.com/pcb-design-guidelines/drilled-holes/
#   https://www.eurocircuits.com/pcb-design-guidelines/mechanical-layer/  (board edge clearance)
# Track width, isolation and annular ring depend on the pattern class (6C, 8D...), which
# Eurocircuits publishes as an image/PDF table, so they are NOT set here: add them to your
# own rules once you pick the class (https://www.eurocircuits.com/pcb-design-guidelines/classification/).
#   drill to drill: 0.25 mm edge to edge of the TOOL size (finished PTH + 0.10 mm), so the
#   finished-hole value below is the same limit as 0.25 mm between tools.
#   copper to routed board edge: 0.25 mm outer layers, 0.40 mm inner layers.
# Later rules win over earlier ones in KiCad, so specific rules come after general ones.

(rule "Eurocircuits hole to hole"
  (constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.25mm)))

(rule "Eurocircuits copper to board edge (outer)"
  (layer outer)
  (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.25mm)))

(rule "Eurocircuits copper to board edge (inner)"
  (layer inner)
  (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.40mm)))
